Article 4 (Certification Services) The Director General of the National Court Administration shall perform the following certification services: <Amended on November 6, 2019>
1. Designation and management of registration authorities;
2. Issuance and renewal of certificates for registration authorities, and for administrative agencies, subsidiary organs, assisting organs, or public officials receiving certification (hereinafter referred to as "subscribing agencies, etc.");
3. Revocation of certificates of registration authorities and subscribing agencies, etc., and preparation of certificate revocation lists;
4. Retention and publication in the system of the certificates of registration authorities and subscribing agencies, etc., and certificate revocation lists;
5. Verification of the validity of certificates of subscribing agencies, etc.;
6. Management of information and records concerning subscribing agencies, etc.;
7. Verification of the identities of registration authorities and subscribers;
8. Time-stamping services and other services considered necessary for a certification authority.
